                         ú ù [ The Story so Far ] ù ú

 FM was formed in February 1995 by me (Necros) and Mellow-D after chatting on
 the phone one day and realizing that starting a good scene music group would
 be both fun and productive for the both of us. I called up Basehead and he
 seemed to be quite pleased with the idea and offered his services. And thus
 with a solitary 'woop' FM was begun. Originally we wanted to call the group
 'o' per Mellow-D's request, but soon we invited Big Jim to join and he
 suggested 'FM' as a name. Luckily by this time we had acquired the perfect
 number of musicians, and the name stuck.

 I quickly released "Realization II" under the FM label, and things began to
 move along nicely. After a few more releases by members, Jak called and said
 he had invited Purple Motion to join. At that time I became aware of just how
 fortuitous it was that both 'four' and 'five' started with the letter 'F'. So
 thus we became Five Musicians.

 Things now were looking great, and Jak released a musicdisk compilation of
 older tunes he had written called 'Kaktoos'. Weeks passed and the FM e-mail
 address was activated at fm@pot.hole.fi (Jak's computer). Unfortunately, we
 realized that Purple Motion was proving to be both unreachable and
 unproductive, so we politely dismissed him from the group.

 Thus we were once again Four Musicians. After languishing in this deplorable
 state for a few more weeks, we came upon a brilliant young musician from OTM
 named Stalker. Listening to his stuff, we realized that we had to snatch up
 this fine young fellow before he fell prey to the sinister lurkings of
 some european demo group. He accepted our invitation, and there was once again
 happiness and joy in the land of the music scene. This bring us to the current
 day, when FM has finally been recognized as a force to be reckoned with. Our
 greetings to all other music groups across the world; we invite you to join us
 in bringing melodic bliss to people worldwide.

                            ú ù [ The Goods ] ù ú

 All the new releases are first uploaded to ftp.mpoli.fi.  After the uploads
 are reviewed and are moved to the correct places, you can find FM-stuff in
 the directory /starport/music/fm.  There should always be an index file in
 the directory, explaining the contents.

 New uploads can also be found on ftp.cdrom.com, in the /demos/music/incoming
 directory.

 Tunes by Necros and Basehead are mirrored also at:

      (ftp) dragon.axs.net :  /pub/demos/songs/necros
                              /pub/demos/songs/basehead

 We have distribution sites, but their numbers are too many to list here.
 Usually most quality boards will carry our releases. Simply check their
 list of affils to see if they are an 'FM Distribution Site'.

